.TH KINTSUGI-SESSION 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-session \- session management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi session
list
.br
.B kintsugi session
show <id>
.br
.B kintsugi session
rename <id> "<title>"
.br
.B kintsugi session
search <query>
.br
.B kintsugi session
fork <id>
.br
.B kintsugi session
export <id>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage sessions: list, view, rename, search, fork, and export.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP \fBlist\fR
Index sessions by title/model/persona/turns
.IP \fBshow\fR
Replay a session log
.IP \fBrename\fR
Set a session's title
.IP \fBsearch\fR
Search transcripts
.IP \fBfork\fR
Copy a session into a new branch
.IP \fBexport\fR
Write a session as legacy JSONL
.SH EXAMPLES
List sessions:
.PP
  $ kintsugi session list
.PP
View a session:
.PP
  $ kintsugi session show abc123
.PP
Rename a session:
.PP
  $ kintsugi session rename abc123 "refactor auth"
.PP
Search sessions:
.PP
  $ kintsugi session search "authentication bug"
.PP
Fork a session:
.PP
  $ kintsugi session fork abc123
.PP
Export as JSONL:
.PP
  $ kintsugi session export abc123
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-run (1)
